                        "canonical_url": null
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "p2",
                        "uuid": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
                        "title": "Removing .env file from Git history",
                        "slug": "removing-env-file-from-git-history",
                        "html": "<p>You committed <code>.env</code>. Everyone has. Here is how to make it go away.</p><h2 id=\"the-fix\">The fix</h2><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card\"><img src=\"__GHOST_URL__/content/images/2023/06/env-leak.png\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"terminal\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"600\" srcset=\"__GHOST_URL__/content/images/size/w600/2023/06/env-leak.png 600w, __GHOST_URL__/content/images/2023/06/env-leak.png 1200w\"></figure><pre><code class=\"language-bash\">git filter-repo --path .env --invert-paths</code></pre><p>Then rotate the keys. The history was public; so were they. See also <a href=\"__GHOST_URL__/how-to-change-the-message-on-last-commit-in-git/amp/\">amending</a> and the <a href=\"__GHOST_URL__/tag/git-filter-repo/\">filter-repo tag</a>.</p><img src=\"https://learn-seo.com/content/images/2024/07/SEO--1-.png\" alt=\"\"><p><a href=\"#/portal/signup\">Subscribe</a> for more.</p><script src=\"https://cdn.example.com/track.js\"></script>",
